From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:49:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] windows.devices.display: Note that an abandoned lock is
 reported once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DLZiLBYev72J1s4D37L7Bi
---
 dlls/windows.devices.display/main.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/windows.devices.display/main.c b/dlls/windows.devices.display/main.c
index 2fc81c2..c8ffd72 100644
--- a/dlls/windows.devices.display/main.c
+++ b/dlls/windows.devices.display/main.c
@@ -479,7 +479,9 @@ static HRESULT lock_display_devices( HANDLE *mutex )
         return S_OK;
     case WAIT_ABANDONED:
         /* The previous owner exited while rebuilding the device nodes, so
-         * they are not known to describe one configuration. */
+         * they are not known to describe one configuration. Only this first
+         * waiter is told; later resolutions acquire the mutex normally and
+         * read whatever win32u's next display cache update leaves. */
         ReleaseMutex( *mutex );
         hr = HRESULT_FROM_WIN32(ERROR_ABANDONED_WAIT_0);
         break;
